body:
PRISM revolve nailed 5-step macro geometry (V=26320.6mm³ EXACT to analytical sum of cylinder volumes) but missed:
(1) drawing convention puts working face on LEFT — preserve part orientation when default Fusion view is rendered;
(2) Detail-A angular features (1° face taper, 3° body taper, 8° base chamfer) are LOAD-BEARING, not decorative;
(3) extrude punches always have central oil hole + cross-drilled relief holes (Ø.05/.06 callouts) — model these by default whenever blueprint title indicates EXTRUDE PUNCH;
(4) tolerances (±.002, +0/-.5° etc.) must be captured on dimensions and propagated to Fusion design parameters, not dropped.
